The function `store_info_in_header` is designed to safely store specific information types into an HTTP header dictionary. It ensures that only valid information types are processed and uses safe string operations to prevent buffer overflows. The function checks if a key already exists in the header dictionary before updating or adding new entries, ensuring data integrity and system stability. This approach effectively mitigates security risks while correctly handling valid input types and safely managing buffer operations.

